// =============================================================================
// VPS Service - Comprehensive CLI API for VPS/VM Management
// =============================================================================
// Purpose: Complete API for the vpsctl command-line tool. This is the largest
// service definition, providing all operations needed for VPS management.
//
// Communication: Unary RPC for all operations
//
// Major Categories:
// - Authentication: Login, OAuth2 device code flow, logout, user info
// - VM Lifecycle: Create, get, list, update, delete, start, stop, restart
// - VM Advanced: Migrate, rebuild, clone, linked clone, console access
// - VM Resources: Hot-add CPU/memory (UpdateVMResources)
// - Disk: Full disk lifecycle (create, attach, resize, detach, delete)
// - Images: Image management from VM or upload
// - Snapshots: Snapshot lifecycle with restore and consolidate
// - Networks: Virtual network CRUD
// - Network Interfaces: NIC management on VMs
// - vSwitch: Virtual switch management
// - Port Groups: Network segmentation with VLAN
// - Public IP: IP allocation and assignment
// - Security Groups: Firewall rules for VMs
// - Templates: Instance templates for repeatable deployments
// - OS Templates: OS definitions from osinfodb
// - Monitoring: Metrics and activity logs
// - Organizations: Multi-tenant management (admin)
// - Users: User management (admin)
// - Datastores: Storage management (DCUI operations)
// - System: Host info, network config, health (DCUI operations)
//
// This is effectively a "monolithic" API that wraps all platform functionality
// for CLI access, as opposed to the more decomposed microservice APIs.
// =============================================================================

